{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Target Spring Framework 6.x with Java 17+ baseline.",
    "Build Kafka support on top of the existing Spring Kafka extension; do not reimplement low-level producer/consumer wrappers.",
    "Expose concurrency and compression as Spring Boot-style configuration properties with sensible global defaults and per-deployment overrides via @ConfigurationProperties.",
    "Implement ACK support through Spring Kafka's AckMode (MANUAL, MANUAL_IMMEDIATE, RECORD, BATCH, COUNT, TIME) plus a thin abstraction so user code can call a domain-specific ack() method.",
    "Implement bindRequestor/bindReplier using Spring Integration's asynchronous request/reply (correlation ID + reply topic) rather than introducing a new messaging paradigm.",
    "Implement batching through Spring Kafka's batch listener container (BatchListenerFactory) with configurable batch size and poll timeout.",
    "Integrate Sqoop as an external process invocation (CLI wrapper) since Sqoop is not JVM-native; abstract it behind a SqoopOperations interface for testability.",
    "Capture Sqoop logs by streaming the process stdout/stderr to SLF4J/Logback via a dedicated appender, including level mapping from Sqoop's log4j categories.",
    "Implement incremental data load by persisting the last-imported value (e.g., lastmodified or a primary-key column) and passing it to Sqoop's --incremental / --last-value parameters.",
    "Use Testcontainers (Kafka container and a Sqoop-mock or local HDFS/SQL target) for the acceptance tests wired into the CI pipeline."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "An experienced senior Java/Spring developer is performing all work, so no ramp-up time is included.",
    "The Spring Kafka extension is already available in the target version; this increment adds new configuration knobs, ACK helpers, request/reply helpers, and batch support on top of it.",
    "Sqoop is invoked as an out-of-process binary; the increment does not port Sqoop into the JVM.",
    "A relational target (e.g., MySQL/Postgres) and a Hadoop/HDFS source exist in the test environment, provided via Testcontainers.",
    "Acceptance tests are implemented in Java using Spring's test framework (JUnit 5) and Testcontainers; no separate BDD tool is required.",
    "Unit testing is included implicitly in each activity and not broken out as a separate WBS item; only the new acceptance-test suite (U1) is a dedicated activity.",
    "Internationalization, security review, and performance benchmarking are out of scope for this increment.",
    "Reference documentation is updated in the same module (Asciidoctor .adoc files) and is treated as a single documentation activity.",
    "Effort is expressed in ideal engineering workdays (8 hours) of focused development by a single developer."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Module setup and API design",
      "activity_description": "Create the new Spring extension module(s) (Kafka and Sqoop), define package layout, public API surfaces (interfaces, configuration classes, builder/factory methods), and the configuration property metadata for global defaults and overrides."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Kafka core producer/consumer wiring",
      "activity_description": "Implement the core KafkaTemplate-based send/receive operations, error handlers, and the default producer/consumer factory configuration used by all other Kafka activities."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Kafka concurrency support",
      "activity_description": "Expose concurrency (number of consumer threads, partitions per consumer) as global default properties with per-deployment overrides; wire to ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Kafka compression support",
      "activity_description": "Add compression type configuration (none, gzip, snappy, lz4, zstd) at the producer level with global defaults and overrides, and document trade-offs."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Kafka ACK support",
      "activity_description": "Provide an ACK API on the message handler/channel so the caller can acknowledge successful processing; map this to AckMode and the underlying Acknowledgment callback, with proper error/retry handling."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Kafka bindRequestor / bindReplier",
      "activity_description": "Implement bindRequestor (producer expecting async replies) and bindReplier (consumer handling requests and sending async replies) using correlation IDs and reply topics, including timeout and error handling."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Kafka batching support",
      "activity_description": "Add a batch listener mode with configurable batch size, poll timeout, and buffer memory; expose a BatchMessageListener abstraction that delivers a List<Record> to user code."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Kafka acceptance test suite (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Set up Testcontainers-based Kafka integration for the CI build, write acceptance tests covering send/receive, concurrency, compression, ACK, request/reply, and batching, and wire them into the build pipeline."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Sqoop job stop support (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Add an API and lifecycle hook to stop a running Sqoop job, including cancellation of the underlying process and cleanup of temporary staging resources at completion time."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Sqoop log capture and streaming (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Identify how Sqoop emits logs, stream stdout/stderr (and Sqoop's own log4j output) into the Spring application's logging mechanism (SLF4J/Logback), with category and level mapping."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Sqoop incremental data load (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement incremental imports: support lastmodified and append modes, persist the last-imported value between runs, and expose it as a configuration property with safe defaults."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Sqoop acceptance test suite",
      "activity_description": "Build Testcontainers-based acceptance tests for stop, log capture, and incremental load against a real Sqoop image and a relational target, and integrate them into CI."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Reference documentation",
      "activity_description": "Author/update Asciidoctor reference docs and code examples for every new configuration property, ACK method, bindRequestor/bindReplier usage, batching, and Sqoop operations."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Integration hardening and bug fixing",
      "activity_description": "End-to-end integration testing, code review feedback, performance tuning of producer/consumer settings, and fixing issues discovered during combined Kafka + Sqoop scenarios."
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 33.0
  }
}
```

